@@ -8,6 +8,10 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates tool input against each tool's registered `inputSchema` (using `ajv`) before calling the executor. When input fails `required`, declared property types, or `enum`, `execute` returns a `ToolResponse` describing the failing field paths and constraints (without echoing or logging offending property values) instead of invoking the executor or throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the rejection back to the model as a `tool_result` for retry within `maxToolRounds`. Static tool schemas are compiled once at `register` time so invalid schemas fail at startup. **Migration note:** an executor that used to hand-validate its input now receives only input the schema already accepts (undeclared extra properties still pass through unmodified), and a tool that relied on seeing malformed input to produce its own error message stops seeing it.
+
